<div class="hero"><div class="fl">📖</div><h1><span class="shine">API Docs</span></h1>
<p class="mut" style="margin:0 0 12px">Version 1 · Base URL <b><%= base %>/api/v1</b></p>
<div class="row"><a class="btn sm" href="/dashboard/api">🔑 My API keys</a></div></div>
<div class="toc sp"><a href="#auth">Authentication</a><a href="#resp">Responses</a><a href="#me">Account</a><a href="#bots">Bots</a><a href="#deploy">Deploy</a><a href="#manage">Manage</a><a href="#pair">Pair code</a><a href="#flow">Full example</a><a href="#errors">Errors</a></div>
<div class="dc">

<h2 id="auth">🔐 Authentication</h2>
<p>Create a key in <a href="/dashboard/api">API Keys</a> and send it with every request:</p>
<pre class="code">Authorization: Bearer dvk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# or
X-API-Key: dvk_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx</pre>
<p class="hint">Requests: JSON bodies (<code>Content-Type: application/json</code>). Limit: 60 requests / minute / key. Keep the key on your server — it can spend your coins.</p>

<h2 id="resp">📦 Responses</h2>
<pre class="code">// success
{ "ok": true, "data": { ... } }

// error
{ "ok": false, "error": { "code": "INSUFFICIENT", "message": "You need 5000 coins to deploy this bot." } }</pre>

<h2 id="me">👤 Account</h2>
<div class="ep"><span class="m g">GET</span><b>/me</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Your name, email and coin balance.</p></div>
<pre class="code">curl <%= base %>/api/v1/me \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_KEY"

{ "ok": true, "data": { "id": "64f...", "name": "Elia", "email": "you@mail.com", "coins": 197930 } }</pre>

<h2 id="bots">🤖 Bots</h2>
<div class="ep"><span class="m g">GET</span><b>/bots</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Bots you can deploy, with price (in coins) and resources.</p></div>
<pre class="code">{ "ok": true, "data": [
  { "id": "65a...", "name": "Mega Bot", "description": "...", "ramMB": 512, "diskMB": 1024,
    "cpuPercent": 0, "priceCoins": 5000, "days": 30, "needsPairCode": true }
] }</pre>

<h2 id="deploy">🚀 Deploy</h2>
<div class="ep"><span class="m p">POST</span><b>/deployments</b>
<p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Buys the bot with your coins and starts the install (takes about a minute).</p>
<table><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th></th></tr><tr><td>botId</td><td>string</td><td>required — id from <code>GET /bots</code></td></tr><tr><td>name</td><td>string</td><td>optional, 3–60 characters</td></tr></table></div>
<pre class="code">curl -X POST <%= base %>/api/v1/deployments \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"botId":"65a...","name":"My WhatsApp bot"}'

// 202
{ "ok": true, "data": { "id": "66b...", "status": "pending", "step": "In queue…", "chargedCoins": 5000, ... } }</pre>
<div class="ep"><span class="m g">GET</span><b>/deployments</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">All your deployments, newest first.</p></div>
<div class="ep"><span class="m g">GET</span><b>/deployments/{id}</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">One deployment: status, install log, events, power state and pair code.</p></div>
<pre class="code">{ "ok": true, "data": {
  "id": "66b...", "name": "My WhatsApp bot", "bot": "Mega Bot",
  "status": "active",            // pending (installing) | active | failed | suspended
  "step": "Your bot is ready.",
  "power": "running",            // running | starting | stopping | offline
  "pairStatus": "need_phone",    // none | need_phone | pairing | code_ready | paired
  "pairCode": "",                // filled when pairStatus = code_ready
  "phone": "", "expiresAt": "2026-11-03T08:00:00.000Z",
  "log": ["› Order received", "✅ Server created", "..."],
  "events": [ { "at": "...", "type": "deploy", "text": "Deploy finished" } ]
} }</pre>
<p class="hint">If the install fails, <code>status</code> becomes <code>failed</code> and your coins are refunded automatically.</p>

<h2 id="manage">⚡ Start / stop / restart</h2>
<div class="ep"><span class="m p">POST</span><b>/deployments/{id}/power</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Body: <code>{"signal":"start"}</code> — signal is <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code> or <code>restart</code>. Works any time while status is <code>active</code>.</p></div>
<pre class="code">curl -X POST <%= base %>/api/v1/deployments/66b.../power \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_KEY" -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"signal":"stop"}'</pre>

<h2 id="pair">📱 Pair code (WhatsApp bots)</h2>
<div class="ep"><span class="m p">POST</span><b>/deployments/{id}/pair</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Body: <code>{"phone":"255712345678"}</code> — country code, digits only (no + and no leading 0). Starts the bot and generates the code.</p></div>
<div class="ep"><span class="m p">POST</span><b>/deployments/{id}/pair/cancel</b><p class="hint" style="margin:6px 0 0">Clears the number and stops waiting, so you can send another number.</p></div>
<p>After <code>/pair</code>, poll <code>GET /deployments/{id}</code> every 2–3 seconds until <code>pairStatus</code> is <code>code_ready</code>, then show <code>pairCode</code> to the customer. In WhatsApp: Settings → Linked devices → Link a device → Link with phone number.</p>

<h2 id="flow">🧪 Full example (Node.js 18+)</h2>
<pre class="code">const BASE = "<%= base %>/api/v1";
const KEY = process.env.DVARY_KEY;
const call = (path, method = "GET", body) =>
  fetch(BASE + path, { method, headers: { Authorization: "Bearer " + KEY, "Content-Type": "application/json" },
                       body: body ? JSON.stringify(body) : undefined }).then(r => r.json());
const wait = (ms) => new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, ms));

const bots = (await call("/bots")).data;
const d = (await call("/deployments", "POST", { botId: bots[0].id, name: "My bot" })).data;

let s;
do { await wait(3000); s = (await call("/deployments/" + d.id)).data; } while (s.status === "pending");
if (s.status !== "active") throw new Error(s.step);

await call("/deployments/" + d.id + "/pair", "POST", { phone: "255712345678" });
do { await wait(3000); s = (await call("/deployments/" + d.id)).data; } while (s.pairStatus !== "code_ready");
console.log("Pair code:", s.pairCode);</pre>
<p><b>Python</b></p>
<pre class="code">import os, time, requests
BASE = "<%= base %>/api/v1"
H = {"Authorization": "Bearer " + os.environ["DVARY_KEY"]}

bots = requests.get(BASE + "/bots", headers=H).json()["data"]
d = requests.post(BASE + "/deployments", headers=H, json={"botId": bots[0]["id"]}).json()["data"]
while True:
    s = requests.get(f"{BASE}/deployments/{d['id']}", headers=H).json()["data"]
    if s["status"] != "pending": break
    time.sleep(3)
print(s["status"], s["step"])</pre>

<h2 id="errors">⚠️ Errors</h2>
<table><tr><th>HTTP</th><th>code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr>
<tr><td>400</td><td>BAD_REQUEST · BAD_NAME · BAD_PHONE · BAD_JSON</td><td>Missing or wrong field</td></tr>
<tr><td>401</td><td>INVALID_KEY</td><td>Missing, wrong or deleted key</td></tr>
<tr><td>402</td><td>INSUFFICIENT</td><td>Not enough coins — add coins on the website</td></tr>
<tr><td>403</td><td>ACCOUNT_DISABLED</td><td>Account is banned</td></tr>
<tr><td>404</td><td>NOT_FOUND</td><td>Bot or deployment not found</td></tr>
<tr><td>409</td><td>ALREADY_HAVE · NOT_READY</td><td>Free bot already deployed / bot not ready yet</td></tr>
<tr><td>429</td><td>RATE_LIMIT</td><td>Too many requests — see <code>Retry-After</code> header</td></tr>
<tr><td>502 / 503</td><td>PAIR_FAILED · NOT_CONFIGURED · MAINTENANCE</td><td>Try again later or contact support</td></tr></table>
</div>
